------------------------------------------------------------------------
             Slackware Post-Install Scripts (PIS) 0.3.0
------------------------------------------------------------------------

               'Let the Slackers be a little bit lazy. ;)'

1. Introduction
===============

PIS is a set of Bash scripts that assists with selected Slackware 15.0
post-installation tasks. Its dialog menus resemble the Slackware installer
and preserve the distribution's transparent, text-file-oriented approach.

PIS does not duplicate Slackware's network or service configuration tools.

2. Features
===========

PIS 0.3.0 can:

 * display the recorded PIS configuration and run a system check;
 * set the locale and console keyboard map;
 * select CLI or GUI login;
 * add users without saving their passwords;
 * activate or deactivate wheel administration after visudo validation;
 * select a system-wide startx session and X keyboard layout;
 * publish installed Huge and Generic kernels to an existing ELILO setup;
 * select a Slackware 15.0 slackpkg mirror by its URL;
 * install and configure selected package-management tools;
 * make automatic backups before changing configuration files;
 * restore earlier files from the PIS menu; and
 * export and apply validated, versioned configuration profiles.

3. Safety and recovery
======================

PIS edits standard Slackware configuration files. Before replacing a file,
version 0.3.0 saves a copy under /var/log/PIS/backups and records it in a
private index. Use the Restore option or run "pis --restore" to recover a
selected copy. The file being replaced during a restore is also backed up.

Depending on the selected operations, PIS can change:

 /etc/profile.d/lang.sh
 /etc/profile.d/lang.csh
 /etc/rc.d/rc.keymap
 /etc/inittab
 /etc/sudoers
 /etc/X11/xinit/xinitrc
 /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d/90-keyboard-layout-evdev.conf
 /etc/slackpkg/mirrors
 /etc/slackpkg/slackpkgplus.conf
 /etc/slapt-get/slapt-getrc
 /boot/efi/EFI/Slackware/elilo.conf

The kernel module only operates when an existing ELILO configuration is
detected. It generates and checks all selected entries before publishing the
new configuration. A resume parameter is included only when active swap is
detected.

4. Profiles
===========

Export the settings recorded by PIS:

 # pis --output workstation.pis

Review, validate and apply a profile:

 # pis --file workstation.pis

Profiles identify their format with PIS_PROFILE_VERSION=1. Mirrors are saved
as URLs instead of line numbers. Only known keys and values are accepted.
Repositories for Slackware-current are rejected by the Slackware 15.0
profile. User passwords are never recorded or exported; a new password is
requested when a profile needs to create an absent user.

Profiles created by PIS 0.2 are deliberately rejected because their user
entry may expose a plaintext password. Create a fresh profile with PIS 0.3.0.

5. Package-management integrations
===================================

PIS uses packages intended for Slackware 15.0 and checks the architecture
before using architecture-specific definitions. It no longer creates links
between incompatible OpenSSL library versions.

Third-party repositories remain optional. Read their documentation and
inspect package origins before installing or upgrading software.

6. Installation and operation
==============================

Build and install PIS with its SlackBuild, then run it as root:

 # installpkg pis-0.3.0-noarch-1_SBo.tgz
 # pis

Options:

 -h, --help          show command help
 -v, --version       show the PIS version
 -c, --check         show the compatibility and configuration check
 -o, --output FILE   export the current profile
 -f, --file FILE     validate and apply a profile
     --restore       open the backup restoration menu

